  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 251 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nAs expected, a light rain event is currently underway across \nportions of northeast Louisiana into southwest MS. Radar and \nsurface observations indicate very light amounts with little to no\nimpact, and the event will be winding down this morning as a weak\nshortwave trough shears eastward across our region. \n\nOtherwise, strong deep layer high pressure will become the primary\ninfluence for our region's weather this week. This is a classic \ndry fall weather pattern with large daily temperature swings,\nseasonably cool at night and mild in the day, and very little \nopportunity for getting rainfall. Model forecasts have trended \nweaker and less amplified with a shortwave trough crossing the \nPlains to MS Valley region this weekend, so the prospects for any \nsignificant rainfall have diminished. Given the extremely dry \nconditions so far this fall season, we will be monitoring wind/RH \nforecasts closely for increased wildfire danger. /EC/",
